<% content_for :title, "Campaigns · Tastatur" %>

<%# A campaign link points at a page on a site this instance measures — that is
    validated, not advisory (CampaignLink#destination_is_a_page_on_this_site) —
    so there is nothing this screen could usefully offer somebody with no sites.
    It says which step is missing rather than rendering an empty builder that
    would refuse everything typed into it. -%>
<div class="shell max-w-2xl">
  <div class="card card-body text-center py-14 mt-8">
    <p class="font-semibold">Add a site first.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mt-2 max-w-md mx-auto">
      A campaign link has to point at a page on a site you measure, so there is nothing to build
      until there is one.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <%= link_to "Sites", sites_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
